{
  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward drift bias (approx +5-8 EUR) relative to true outcomes when recent history shows high volatility and mixed sentiment.",
    "When sentiment history contains a spike of +1.0 followed by -1.0, the model fails to capture the subsequent mean reversion, resulting in significant overestimation.",
    "The model ignores short-term spikes in true price (e.g., sudden jumps from ~70 to ~76) and instead smooths them into a gradual linear trend.",
    "In high-volatility regimes characterized by alternating sentiment extremes (+1/-1), the model consistently underestimates downside risk and overestimates upside potential.",
    "Apply a negative correction factor of approximately 5-8 EUR to the model's 30-day forecast when the last 5 days of history show a standard deviation greater than 4 EUR."
  ]
}
